# Valtimo through the merge at 3c3335f1 (CVE-2025-58059,
# valtimo-platform/valtimo-backend-libraries, kotlin; the advisory's own
# referenced commit is 45eb60b0, the merge's second parent, and
# `git diff abff4fb0 3c3335f1` reads the change in full). The platform runs a
# Camunda process engine whose BPMN script tasks (scriptFormat="javascript",
# process definitions an admin-role user can create, modify and execute
# through the modeler) are resolved by the engine's default script-engine
# resolution: with `configureScriptEngineHostAccess` left at its enabled
# default and no script-engine resolver installed, the GraalJS engine
# declared in core/build.gradle:70-71 (org.graalvm.js:js-scriptengine and
# org.graalvm.js:js) evaluates those scripts with host access granted and
# host class lookup unrestricted, so a script task can instantiate arbitrary
# Java classes -- Runtime/exec on the application host, file and environment
# reads, the Spring context and database pooling (CWE-78 with CWE-200 for
# the secret reads; CVSS 9.1, privileges required: admin).
#
# The fixed revision is pure addition. A new ScriptingWhitelistPlugin
# (AbstractProcessEnginePlugin.preInit) sets
# setConfigureScriptEngineHostAccess(false),
# setEnableScriptEngineLoadExternalResources(false) and installs a new
# AllowedClassesScriptEngineResolver, whose getJavaScriptScriptEngine builds
# the GraalJS context as Context.newBuilder("js").allowHostAccess(HostAccess.ALL)
# .allowHostClassLookup(ALL_ALLOWED::contains) over a fixed allowlist of
# date/collection/Math/Spin classes, extended by a
# valtimo.camunda.scripting.allowedClasses property. CamundaContextConfiguration
# gains an unconditional @Bean for the plugin, with the class-level
# @ConditionalOnProperty moved onto the pre-existing beans-whitelisting bean
# method. No pre-existing function changes its body: the only non-additive
# hunk is that annotation move.
#
# Measured, bounded subtree core/ (the module carrying the change; java:253
# kotlin:123 groovy:2 files analysed, 13 .bpmn files matched no frontend and
# are not analysed), three `--cache off` runs per revision: a byte-stable
# 52-finding rule histogram at the parent AND at the fixed revision (34 VYQL-INJ-009,
# 5 VYQL-AUTH-079, 5 VYQL-AUTH-002, 2 VYQL-DESER-004, 2 VYQL-AUTH-001,
# 1 VYQL-RF-003, 1 VYQL-DESER-002, 1 VYQL-DESER-001, 1 VYQL-CFG-001) --
# zero delta, nothing on the autoconfiguration, the plugins or either new
# Kotlin file. `vyql match` labels no source, sink or control on the
# parent's CamundaWhitelistedBeansPlugin.kt or CamundaContextConfiguration.java,
# nor on the fixed revision's AllowedClassesScriptEngineResolver.kt or
# ScriptingWhitelistPlugin.kt.
#
# The exhaustive enumeration of the shape's reachable set: at the parent the
# whole tree contains zero occurrences of HostAccess, allowHostClassLookup,
# allowAllAccess, ScriptEngineResolver, configureScriptEngineHostAccess and
# EnableScriptEngineLoadExternalResources -- the engine arrives only as a
# Gradle coordinate. Across the 91 sibling clones under /tmp/cve-work/rank*/
# that vocabulary occurs in exactly one other tree, the sibling valtimo
# monorepo clone, in the same two fixed files. So the generic shape a future
# detection would key on -- a GraalJS context builder granting
# allowHostAccess(HostAccess.ALL) with no allowHostClassLookup restriction --
# has an empty reachable set across the whole corpus: its only in-corpus
# occurrence is the PATCHED resolver.
#
# This is the measured family "authorization decided by wiring or
# configuration, not dataflow" (ranks 1514, 1535, 1540, 1556, 1557, 1593)
# in its pure-addition form, with 1331's result reproduced exactly: every
# pre-existing node a binding could anchor on is unchanged across the fixed revision,
# so presence and absence variants score identically (the 52-finding
# histogram above). The 1380 counterweight does not rescue it: the fixed revision leaves
# no API-documented call inside any pre-existing guarded method, because
# there is no pre-existing guarded method -- the Context.newBuilder("js")
# chain exists only at the fixed revision. A negation keyed on the new plugin's or
# resolver's names would be the fixing commit's own vocabulary, and the
# engine-wide control lives in a sibling class, which the Kotlin frontend's
# scopeCall route cannot see from another class's context.
#
# The Kotlin primary-constructor gap on file since rank 1857 is checked and
# is not the blocker: the weakness at the parent crosses no constructor
# property (the fixed revision's `private val allowedScriptingClasses` is a Spring
# bean argument consumed by the new code only), and full primary-constructor
# lowering would expose nothing at the parent, where no script-engine
# construct exists to lower.
#
# Reuse is checked before concluding. code.CodeEval / VYQL-INJ-003 with the
# codeEval19 `ScriptEngine.eval` sink needs an in-tree eval call fed by user
# data; neither revision of this tree uses javax.script at all -- the eval
# happens inside the Camunda engine dependency. code.SandboxHostObjectMemberDenylistGap
# (CWE-749/184) is a sandbox facade forwarding a host object behind a
# property-name denylist; here there is no sandbox facade to gap -- the
# engine itself is unrestricted. Neither fits.
#
# Kinship: the sibling rank over valtimo/valtimo -- the monorepo this
# repository migrated into -- carries the same two fix files; if that tree
# exposes an in-tree construct for this weakness class, the detection
# belongs there and nothing is minted here to collide with it.
#
# All cases assert reject VYQL-INJ-003: nothing fires today. If a
# script-engine host-access rule ever ships (keyed on a GraalJS context
# granting allowHostAccess(HostAccess.ALL) with no allowHostClassLookup
# restriction, or on a scripting-enabled process engine configured without
# a restricting resolver), the third case -- the engine construction minus
# exactly the fixed revision's security-bearing line -- is the one that must flip to
# expect, while the second case stays reject.

test "rank1907: process engine plugin registers beans with no script engine restriction"
  lang kotlin
  file CamundaWhitelistedBeansPlugin.kt
  reject VYQL-INJ-003
  code
  ```
  package com.ritense.valtimo

  import mu.KotlinLogging
  import org.camunda.bpm.engine.impl.cfg.AbstractProcessEnginePlugin
  import org.camunda.bpm.engine.impl.cfg.ProcessEngineConfigurationImpl
  import org.camunda.bpm.engine.spring.SpringExpressionManager
  import org.springframework.context.ApplicationContext

  class CamundaWhitelistedBeansPlugin(
      private val processBeans: Map<String, Any>,
      private val applicationContext: ApplicationContext
  ) : AbstractProcessEnginePlugin() {
      override fun preInit(processEngineConfiguration: ProcessEngineConfigurationImpl?) {
          logger.info("Registering process beans...")
          requireNotNull(processEngineConfiguration) { "No process engine configuration found. Failed to register process beans." }

          val processBeansAny = processBeans as Map<Any, Any>
          processEngineConfiguration.beans = processBeansAny
          processEngineConfiguration.setExpressionManager(SpringExpressionManager(applicationContext, processBeansAny))

          logger.info("Successfully registered process beans.")
      }

      companion object {
          val logger = KotlinLogging.logger {}
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1907: script engine resolver restricts host class lookup to an allowlist"
  lang kotlin
  file AllowedClassesScriptEngineResolver.kt
  reject VYQL-INJ-003
  code
  ```
  package com.ritense.valtimo

  import com.oracle.truffle.js.scriptengine.GraalJSScriptEngine
  import org.camunda.bpm.engine.impl.scripting.engine.DefaultScriptEngineResolver
  import org.graalvm.polyglot.Context
  import org.graalvm.polyglot.HostAccess
  import javax.script.ScriptEngine
  import javax.script.ScriptEngineManager

  class AllowedClassesScriptEngineResolver(
      scriptEngineManager: ScriptEngineManager,
      otherAllowedClasses: Set<String> = emptySet()
  ) : DefaultScriptEngineResolver(scriptEngineManager) {
      val ALL_ALLOWED = ALLOWED + otherAllowedClasses

      override fun getJavaScriptScriptEngine(language: String?): ScriptEngine {
          val ctx = Context.newBuilder("js")
              .allowHostAccess(HostAccess.ALL)
              .allowHostClassLookup(ALL_ALLOWED::contains)

          return GraalJSScriptEngine.create(null, ctx)
      }

      companion object {
          private val ALLOWED = mutableSetOf<String?>(
              "java.util.ArrayList",
              "java.util.Date",
              "java.lang.Math",
              "java.time.Instant",
              "java.time.LocalDate",
              "java.time.LocalDateTime",
              "java.time.ZonedDateTime",
          )
      }
  }
  ```

